4. Physical Attribution:
   This bias is physically distinguishable as a known ERA5 nocturnal boundary-layer warm bias caused by ECMWF over-mixing stable nocturnal boundary layers. It CANNOT be attributed to lapse-rate error because coastal stations (Karwar, Honavar, Panjim), where Delta_z < 90 m and lapse adjustments are < 0.6 °C, exhibit warm biases up to -2.44 °C.

